id: i2c
package: platform_core
label: I2C
description: >
  This is an I2C HLD Driver that supports both master and slave modes in
  both blocking and non-blocking types of transfers.

  This component is instantiable, meaning that several named instances can be
  created. For each instance a configuration is generated along with an
  initialization struct set according to this configuration. These instance
  defines and variables are available in a generated header file,
  sl_i2c_instances.h.

  If the Services->Runtime->System Setup->sl_main component is included in
  a project, the driver instances will be initialized automatically, using the
  instance configurations, during the sli_main_init() call in main.c or in the
  start task when using an RTOS.

  Selecting this component will include the I2C Core component,
  which is the implementation of the I2C driver itself.
category: Platform|Driver|I2C
quality: evaluation
metadata:
  sbom:
    license: Zlib
root_path: platform_core/platform/driver/i2c
instantiable:
  prefix: instance
config_file:
- path: "config/s2/sl_i2c_{{instance}}_config.h"
  file_id: i2c_config
  condition: [device_series_2]
- path: "config/s3/sl_i2c_{{instance}}_config.h"
  file_id: i2c_config
  condition: [device_series_3]
provides:
- name: i2c
  allow_multiple: true
requires:
- name: i2c_core
template_contribution:
- name: i2c_instances
  value: "{{instance}}"
